Or, the Tragic Fate of the invisible Storm.

This is my third ascension, and the first with a "conduct". I admit I
made it pretty easy on myself by allowing shields, but this way she was
able to follow the conduct from the first first move, and shields aren't
really clothing, are they?

I played this game over several days and didn't keep notes, so I really
don't remember much of the earliest part, she dipped for Excalibur and
ran into several bones levels early on, at least one being a previous 
incarnation of herself and one each of archaeologist and a wizard.

She bought some protection in Minetown and prayed for a little more,
only to screw up by praying too soon once and lose it all again. Yikes I
didn't know that would happen.

She was able to get most of the loot IDed fairly early thanks to a
little luck with blessed ID scrolls. She genocided c before meeting more
than a few of them (too much danger, and no benefit for a nudist). Only
afterwards did I realize she could have made a few stoning grenades 
first since she had a =oPC. She did put that to good use however, by 
turning herself into a silver dragon and laying an egg. The resulting 
hatchling was named Storm.

Once he got bigger she retrieved a saddle from her Minetown stash rode
him for most of the rest of the game. (They must have been quite a
sight.) She wished for the Magic Mirror of Merlin as soon as she got a
chance (from a throne, IIRC). By this time she'd seen at least one
artifact besides Excalibur so I knew it wasn't a sure thing, but she got
it. She then went and sacrificed for Mojo. Sokoban had held a bag, so 
she still had no reflection.

She got a Shield of Reflection from the Medusa level and I blew it up
remarkably fast. (It was +4 and I (r)ead instead of (d)ropping a ?oEA.)

The the valk quest was fairly uneventful though this was my first time
finishing it. She had no major problems in the castle, and after
clearing it out, spent a /long/ time organizing her inventory, doing
alchemy, trying to re-get protection (did better this time but 
accidentally got crowned before reaching anything too impressive), poly 
piling and all that kind of management stuff. She got her second ring of 
strength charged so she could finally throw Mojo. Fun, but probably not 
all that useful. It got blown up before too long anyway. She also wished 
for a +oID, having suffered brain damage at one point and not wanting to 
relearn everything the hard way.

She used an "extra" wish from a smoky potion to get a new shield of
reflection. Ironically it wasn't long after that I realized she was
was better off discarding it and wielding a second weapon.

Finished exploring Gehennom, did more management stuff before taking on
the Wizard. She had no major trouble there, but in the  Sanctum
"the invisible Storm" (as he was now refered to be the game) got his 
saddle cursed, while she was in it. She was stuck. I didn't know that 
could happen, or have any clue how to fix it. (Blessed remove curse 
didn't help.) A purple worm plucked her off eventually, but I still 
couldn't figure out how to uncurse the saddle. And now she couldn't get 
back on. Never the less, they made their way back up with the amulet. 
And then the most annoying Nethack incident not actually resulting in 
YASD I have ever experienced, happened:

Along comes a black pudding. It somehow got into a position between her
and Storm, so when she bashed it, it "split" through a wall. So she
kills the one on this side and teleports to dispatch the other, only to
find a snake instead. At this point I should have realized what was
about to happen, but I didn't. She kills the snake and behold, it's a
chameleon. This gives her an idea for uncursing the saddle. So she puts
on her =oPC, eats the chameleon and turns herself into a succubus. Now
maybe she can steal the saddle and uncurse it! So she warps back over to
Storm... who, just at that moment eats the /other/ chameleon corpse. Yep
the black pudding was a chameleon, all along. Storm turns into something
totally helpless. Ironically that does get the saddle off (oh joy).

So she hits him with a potion of polymorph. Now he's a Shocking
Sphere(!). Not admitting defeat, she put down the amulet, warped up to
the Castle and wrested a final charge from a wand of polymorph to turn 
him into... an ape. She knew of no polymorph traps, and at this point, 
she really should have given up, but you have to remember Storm was not 
only her trusted steed and companion but her child. Her next plan was to
reverse genocide chameleons and feed them to him. But she didn't have
cursed ?oG or any Unholy Water. She tried to make some in the Valley of
the Dead (really dumb plan) not only did she lose protection, it didn't
work either. At this point the Wizard is starting to get annoying so she
decides she has no choice but to continue her quest without Storm.

She warps back to level 38 and brings the amulet up to the castle.
Storm is still tame, so she figure the least she can do is drop him off
on level 1 (knowing he would never survive the planes). Sadly it was
not to be. I'm still not 100% sure what happened but I think he died and 
and was consumed the hungry void on the Rogue Level . It's possible he 
hit level teleporter instead I suppose. But even FJola was not about to
search all through the dungeon for him at this point.

Heartbroken but committed to Tyr's holy quest, she makes her way
to level 1. There she uses up the castle wand to get a magic marker (to
charge up some rings and such (Meaning she could again throw Mojo, for
what that's worth), and a blessed figurine of ki-rin.

She activated figurine, saddled it and named it Cyclone. She even 
summoned a swarm of acid blobs so it could get it's HP up a little 
before the final test. Her own HP was over 550 but her AC was 10, I 
wasn't sure what would happen. There were no priests living by this 
point and as the Hand of Elbereth with the Wizard after her, praying 
didn't seem workable either.

Well, earth went fine. She used scrolls of Scare Monster on air, that
worked nicely except for dragons. There was a black dragon that she was
afraid might disintegrate she steed, but she canceled it. Then a Red
Dragon burned a scroll once.  None of that was a really bad problem. No
the problem was once again, a dumb mistake. She tried to pick up and
eat some heavy monster just before stepping through the portal (Hey, I
thought there was no gravity!*) Anyway a Jabberwock killed the ki-rin 
she was riding before she could do anything. And of course "A"s don't 
leave corpses so her wand of undead turning was no use.

*Speaking of strange physics, how come she got pushed backwards when she 
threw Mojollnir? That doesn't normally apply when riding a flying creature.

On the plane of fire, she made one last attempt to get a mount since she
still had the saddle. She did a confused mass-tame which included an
orange dragon who she named Smog (not to be confused with Smaug). Well
she got the saddle on him, but couldn't seem to climb on. Still
confused, oops. Smog apparently was annoyed by all this fumbling and
refused to accompany her further, but she did get some random fire
creatures out of the deal.

The salamanders seemed to enjoy boiling water elementals, but I'm not
sure how much that helped. I thought she was safe from eels with
her "oMB, forgetting that the electric ones could blow things up.
There goes the ring of strength again, plus a wand of death. Grrr. She 
used her last ?oGD and a charge of the Orb of Fate to track down the portal.

On Astral, she used the acid blob swarm technique. She also had a
blessed figurine of a purple worm she meant activated at this point but
forgot about it. No need though, the acid blobs did their job and with a
little /oTele use she made it to the first altar with no trouble, Boom,
it's Lawful.

